schema:description:
This capability allows for the granular and real-time management of patient permissions for data sharing. It enables patients to grant, revoke, or modify access rights for different providers and purposes.&#xD;
&#xD;
The purpose is to place the patient in control of their data and ensure that sharing is always based on explicit, informed consent. This is a key requirement for building trust and complying with privacy laws.&#xD;
&#xD;
Example: A "consent dashboard" where a patient can give a specialist access to their history for only a 24-hour window.&#xD;
